{"name":"Natural Almond","hex":"#ded2bb","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"natural","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Existing in nature.\nExisting in the nature of a person or thing; innate, not acquired or learned. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","Existing in the nature of a person or thing; innate, not acquired or learned. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A native inhabitant of a place, country, etc.","A note that is not or is no longer to be modified by an accidental."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/natural"},{"term":"almond","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The seed within the drupe of a small deciduous tree in family Rosaceae, Prunus amygdalus, considered a culinary nut.","The tree that produces almonds."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Brownish, resembling the colour of an almond nut."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/almond"}],"entries":[{"title":"Nature","blocks":[{"text":"Nature, in the broadest sense, is the physical world or universe. In this general sense nature refers to the laws, elements and phenomena of the physical world, including life. Although humans are part of nature, human activity or humans as a whole are often described as at times at odds, or outright separate and even superior to nature."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/06/Startrails_above_Gunung_Bromo_-_Indonesia.jpg/330px-Startrails_above_Gunung_Bromo_-_Indonesia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nature"},{"title":"Almond","blocks":[{"text":"The almond is a species of tree from the genus Prunus. Along with the peach, it is classified in the subgenus Amygdalus, distinguished from the other subgenera by corrugations on the woody shell (endocarp) surrounding the seed."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thu